course: dictionary
lesson: 14398
title: Outnumber: more in number
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To outnumber someone or something means to be more in number. Outnumber is a verb: outnumber, outnumbers, outnumbered, outnumbering. The word is made of out and number: one group goes beyond the other in how many there are.
explain: «There are 12 girls and 8 boys in our class, so the girls outnumber the boys.» The girls are the bigger group. You can also say how many more: «The girls outnumber the boys by 4.» Twelve take away eight is four.
explain: In stories, a smaller group can still win. «The army was outnumbered, but it still won the battle.» Here the army had fewer soldiers than the other side, so it was outnumbered.
fact: Outnumber means to be more in number than another group.
fact: «The girls outnumber the boys by 4» means there are 4 more girls than boys.
fact: Bigger = smaller + difference. If a group is outnumbered by 4, the bigger group is the smaller group plus 4.
fact: «Outnumber 3 to 1» means one group is three times as big as the other, for example 3 children for every 1 adult.
fact: Phrases to remember: outnumber by, outnumber … to …, and be outnumbered.
exercise: «There are 15 cats and 9 dogs at the shelter, so the cats outnumber the dogs.» What does outnumber mean here? | Are happier than | Are fewer in number than | Are the same number as | *Are more in number than
exercise: «Ten children and six adults went on the trip.» How many more children than adults were there? | 6 | 3 | 16 | *4
exercise: «The rebels were outnumbered 3 to 1 by the king's army.» Which side had more soldiers? | Nobody knows | *The king's army | The rebels | Both sides were the same
test: If there are 7 red balls and 2 blue balls, which colour outnumbers the other? | Blue | Neither | Both are equal | *Red
test: «The team of 4 was outnumbered by a team of 9.» Which team had fewer players? | The team of 9 | Both teams had 4 | Neither | *The team of 4
exam: Ben has 3 blue marbles and 8 red marbles. By how many do the red marbles outnumber the blue ones? | 11 | *5 | 24 | 3
